From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:13:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Read a template world's block ids and light from a mapped
 section store

A pinned match map held its sections' ids and light on the heap: 25 to 48 MB, about 85% of what a
loaded map costs, which sized the heap for the largest map and cut that map's square to fit.
AthenaSectionStore writes them once per template, into athena-sections-<fingerprint>.bin next to
the region files, and maps the file read only. A section reads its ids and light in place; the
first write to either copies that part onto the heap. Mortal_Skies at radius 300: the map's live
heap 47-56 MB -> 14-15 MB. The page cache holds the file once for every server on the box.

The store is built in the background the first time a template loads, or ahead of time with
java -cp <patched jar> net.minecraft.server.v1_8_R3.AthenaSectionStore <maps>. The ids go through
ChunkRegionLoader.athenaSectionIds, the conversion a load from NBT uses, and the index audit
compares the two at load (0 mismatches over Mortal_Skies, Par_72).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

